<%# Terms of use, the English translation. %>
<section>
  <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>These terms of use (the "Terms") govern access to and use of Fitora, an online management software for gyms, studios and clubs (the "Service"). The Customer accepts them at their first sign-in; using the Service means accepting the Terms.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>2. Publisher</h2>
  <p>The Service is published by <%= legal_identity(tax_label: "tax ID") %>. Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= legal_contact %>"><%= legal_contact %></a><% if issuer.phone.present? %>, <%= issuer.phone %><% end %>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>3. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Customer</strong>: the person or business that runs one or more gyms and for whom Fitora has opened an administrator account.</li>
    <li><strong>User</strong>: anyone who signs in to the Service on the Customer's behalf (administrator, front desk, coach).</li>
    <li><strong>Member</strong>: a member of the Customer's gym, whose details the Customer records, and who may be given access to the member app.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>4. Account and access</h2>
  <p>The Customer's account is created by Fitora, which sends them their credentials by email. At their first sign-in, the Customer confirms their address, replaces the temporary password with their own and accepts these Terms. The Customer can then open further gyms from their account.</p>
  <p>The Customer is responsible for their Users' credentials and for what is done with them. They create their team's access and give each the appropriate role.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>5. Features, updates and information</h2>
  <p>The account gives access to every feature of the Service. Updates apply to every Customer, with nothing for them to do, and are presented in the account's "What's New" page. Fitora may email the account's administrator about the Service and their contract.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>6. Commercial terms</h2>
  <p>Financial terms are agreed directly between Fitora and the Customer, outside the Service, which involves no payment to or invoicing by Fitora.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>7. The Customer's commitments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the Service lawfully and in accordance with these Terms.</li>
    <li>Enter accurate information, and record about Members only what is needed to manage their membership.</li>
    <li>Tell Members how their data is processed and obtain their explicit consent where the law requires it, in particular for health information and photos.</li>
    <li>Not attempt to reach another gym's data, nor disrupt the Service.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>8. Members' data</h2>
  <p>The Customer remains the controller of their Members' data; Fitora processes it on the Customer's behalf, only to provide the Service, and never sells or transfers it. The details are in the <a href="/confidentialite">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>9. Availability and support</h2>
  <p>Fitora takes reasonable steps to keep the Service available around the clock, except for maintenance, a supplier's incident or force majeure. The Customer can reach support from their account (Support). Data is backed up every day.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>The Service, its code, texts and graphics belong to the publisher. The Customer receives a personal, non-exclusive right to use it for the length of their contract with Fitora. The data the Customer enters remains theirs.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>11. Liability</h2>
  <p>Fitora is bound by an obligation of means. It is not liable for indirect damage (loss of revenue, of customers…), nor for decisions the Customer takes from the Service's information. In any event, Fitora's liability is limited to the amounts the Customer paid to Fitora over the last twelve months.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>12. Term, termination and getting the data back</h2>
  <p>The account stays open for the length agreed between Fitora and the Customer. Fitora may suspend access to the Service under the conditions agreed with the Customer; no data is deleted because of the suspension. On request, Fitora gives the Customer a copy of its data. Also on request, Fitora deletes the account and its data, except what it must keep by law.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>13. Changes to the Terms</h2>
  <p>Fitora may change the Terms; the new version is published on this page and the Customer is told. Using the Service after it takes effect means accepting it.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>The Terms are governed by Tunisian law. Failing an amicable settlement, any dispute falls under the competent courts of Tunis.</p>
</section>
